── detail · template ──
AS YOU TYPE
:run_passed: mentions the group picked under user group (in the review channel); posts: Review please <!subteam^S0REVIEW01>: <https://git.example/acme/team-a/api/-/merge_requests/263|mr> Add a stats endpoint for the dashboard

The message. {group} and {@handle} are sent as Slack's mention of the group's id, so they ping, and only in the review channel. With several merge requests, a placeholder that names one gives their different values joined by commas. :name: is an emoji.

ACCEPTS
text with {mrs} or {link}, and any of:
{mrs}      each request; bullets for several
{count}    2
{group}    @review-squad, mentioned
{@handle}  a group by its handle, mentioned
{link}     mr, linked; api !263 for several
{url}      its address
{repo}     api
{project}  acme/team-a/api
{iid}      263
{title}    Add a stats endpoint for the dashboard
{branch}   stats-endpoint
{target}   main
{author}   vimes
{tickets}  its ticket keys, linked

NOW
{group} :gitlab: {mrs}

WITH A SAMPLE MERGE REQUEST
Review please @review-squad: mr <https://git.example/acme/team-a/api/-/merge_requests/263> Add a stats endpoint for the dashboard

WITH TWO
Review please @review-squad:
• api !263 <https://git.example/acme/team-a/api/-/merge_requests/263> Add a stats endpoint for the dashboard
• web !12 <https://git.example/acme/team-a/web/-/merge_requests/12> Show the stats

